            {
              "text": "When selecting a consultancy in Adelaide for **business workflow automation** and **Microsoft Power Automate implementation**, the right fit depends largely on the size of your organisation, whether you need enterprise-level governance (Center of Excellence), and your integration requirements (e.g., SharePoint, Dynamics 365, or legacy ERPs).\n\nThe leading consultancies with a strong presence and proven track record in Adelaide include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Dedicated Adelaide-Grown Consultancies & Specialists\n\n*   **Comunet**\n    *   **Focus:** Mid-market, local councils, healthcare, and enterprise business process digitisation.\n    *   **Why them:** Headquartered on South Terrace in Adelaide, Comunet has over 30 years of local history. They excel at Microsoft Modern Workplace transformations, using Power Automate, Power Apps, and SharePoint to replace manual paperwork, approval bottlenecks, and disconnected legacy routines. \n    *   **Best for:** Organisations wanting a local, hands-on partner for end-to-end process digitisation and practical workflow automation.\n\n*   **Chamonix (Synechron)**\n    *   **Focus:** Enterprise architecture, state government, utilities, and large-scale digital transformation.\n    *   **Why them:** Chamonix is an Adelaide-founded consulting powerhouse known for architecting large, complex solutions (regularly trusted by SA Water, SA Health, and other SA Government departments). If your workflow automation requires rigorous security frameworks, integration into complex data environments, or cloud architecture, their senior consultants are among the best in South Australia.\n    *   **Best for:** Complex, regulated environments and public sector organisations requiring enterprise-grade solution architecture.\n\n*   **Concept Data**\n    *   **Focus:** Small to mid-sized businesses (SMBs) and mid-market modern workplace automation.\n    *   **Why them:** Based in Eastwood and Mount Barker, Concept Data specialises in deploying practical Microsoft Power Platform solutions, including Power Automate flows, SharePoint structure design, and custom front-end apps. They focus on eliminating operational friction and routine manual data entry without over-engineering the solution.\n    *   **Best for:** Mid-tier commercial businesses looking for agile, direct-access consulting and fast turnaround times.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Major National Microsoft Partners with Strong Adelaide Offices\n\n*   **Data#3 (King William St, Adelaide)**\n    *   **Focus:** Enterprise, education, and government digital transformation.\n    *   **Why them:** As one of Microsoft’s largest and most accredited Solutions Partners in Australia, Data#3 has an extensive dedicated Business Applications and Modern Work team in Adelaide. They do more than just build individual flows; they help organisations implement **Center of Excellence (CoE)** governance models, manage Power Automate licensing, and deploy Robotic Process Automation (RPA) and AI Builder models.\n    *   **Best for:** Enterprise-wide automation rollouts where data loss prevention (DLP), governance, and licensing control are critical.\n\n*   **Datacom (Adelaide CBD & Modbury Hub)**\n    *   **Focus:** Large commercial, government, and council workflow modernisations.\n    *   **Why them:** Datacom has a significant footprint in South Australia. Their local Information Management and Intelligent Workplace consultants specialise in building robust automation pipelines—connecting Microsoft 365, Dataverse, Copilot Studio, and Power Automate to orchestrate multi-department processes.\n    *   **Best for:** Large organisations looking for high-capacity delivery and ongoing managed support.\n\n*   **Engage Squared (Adelaide & National presence)**\n    *   **Focus:** Employee experience, Modern Work, and collaboration-centric automation.\n    *   **Why them:** A premier Microsoft Modern Work partner across Australia, Engage Squared focuses heavily on human-centred workflow automation. If your workflow challenges centre around Microsoft Teams approvals, SharePoint records management, or employee lifecycle workflows, they are market leaders in driving actual user adoption.\n    *   **Best for:** People-driven workflows, approval chains, and governance-heavy document management systems.\n\n---\n\n### Key Questions to Ask When Selecting a Consultancy:\n\n1. **How do you handle Governance and Data Loss Prevention (DLP)?** \n   Unregulated Power Automate implementations can cause \"flow sprawl\" and shadow IT. Ensure they establish an Environment and DLP strategy from day one.\n2. **Will you build Cloud Flows, Desktop RPA, or both?**\n   If your workflows need to interact with modern APIs (like Xero, Salesforce, or Microsoft 365), Cloud Flows suffice. If you need to interact with legacy on-premise software without APIs, verify their experience with **Power Automate Desktop (RPA)**.\n3. **What is your handover and enablement model?**\n   The best consultancies will train your internal power users to maintain standard flows rather than locking you into expensive minor support retainers for simple logic adjustments.",
